Subject: [PATCH] display: a forced scale factor sets the page's pixel ratio

With --force-device-scale-factor the browser window, the compositor and
the Sec-CH-DPR header all use the forced scale, but ScreenInfo still took
the profile's ratio. On a Windows host at 150% launched with
--force-device-scale-factor=1.5, a persona with ratio 1 read
devicePixelRatio 1, the page was rastered at 1x into a 1.5x window and the
OS stretched it, so text was blurred, and the DPR header said 1.5 while
JavaScript said 1.

When a scale factor is forced, ScreenInfo keeps the display's own (forced)
factor, so the page ratio, raster scale, window scale and Sec-CH-DPR are
one value. Without the switch the profile's ratio applies as before. The
composed profile is unchanged, so a seed keeps its machine.

diff --git a/ui/display/display_util.cc b/ui/display/display_util.cc
index 0459e08..cee1ff9 100644
--- a/ui/display/display_util.cc
+++ b/ui/display/display_util.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,13 @@ void DisplayUtil::DisplayToScreenInfo(ScreenInfo* screen_info,
                               *profile->screen_avail_height());
         screen_info->available_rect = available;
       }
-      if (profile->device_scale_factor().has_value()) {
+      // A forced scale factor is the scale the window is drawn at. The browser
+      // window, the compositor and the Sec-CH-DPR header already use it, so a
+      // profile ratio here would leave the page alone at another scale: drawn
+      // at 1x into a 1.5x window and stretched by the OS, and a
+      // devicePixelRatio that disagrees with the header.
+      if (profile->device_scale_factor().has_value() &&
+          !Display::HasForceDeviceScaleFactor()) {
         screen_info->device_scale_factor = *profile->device_scale_factor();
       }
       if (profile->screen_color_depth().has_value()) {
